      "instance_name": "anti_latino_hispanic_stereotypes",
      "label": "Anti-Latino/Hispanic Stereotypes",
      "description": "The meme relies on the harmful stereotype that Latinos are pests or vermin (specifically, 'roaches') that should be eradicated ('raided'), which is a common racist trope used to dehumanize and justify discrimination against Latinos. This stereotype is part of a broader pattern of anti-Latino racism that includes associations with criminality, uncleanliness, and being a burden on society.",
